0 < 1 ---
1 < 1 name: delete-comment
2 < 1 description: Use when the operator runs "/delete-comment [path...]" or asks to sweep, triage or delete code comments. Categorises every comment (tautology, stale, excuse, decision), deletes them, files an issue per excuse, moves decisions into docs/adr/, and ratchets lint/comments-baseline.json down.
3 < 1 argument-hint: "[path...]"
4 < 1 allowed-tools: Read Grep Glob Bash Edit Write Agent AskUserQuestion
5 < 1 ---
6 < 1 
7 < 1 # /delete-comment
8 < 1 
9 < 1 This repository keeps no comments. `lint/comments.py` counts comment lines per tracked source
10 < 1 file and `tests/test_comment_ratchet.py` holds every file at or below
11 < 1 `lint/comments-baseline.json`. This skill lowers that baseline: every comment it can judge
12 < 1 leaves, and what it knew goes somewhere better.
13 < 1 
14 < 1 | Category | What it is | Action |
15 < 1 |---|---|---|
16 < 1 | `tautology` | repeats what the code says | delete |
17 < 1 | `stale` | describes code, behaviour or history that is no longer true, or history git holds | delete |
18 < 1 | `excuse` | licenses a hack: workaround, "for now", TODO, swallowed error, magic retry | delete, file one issue per hack |
19 < 1 | `decision` | an important, non-obvious decision the code cannot show | delete, record in an ADR |
20 < 1 | `keep` | load-bearing text, or undecided | leave; the ratchet holds it |
21 < 1 
22 < 1 Pragmas (`#!`, `@ts-`, `eslint-`, `noqa`, `type: ignore`, inline `@type` casts) are not comments
23 < 1 to the lint and are never touched. Vendored code (`vendor/`, `pouf/`) and fixtures are out of
24 < 1 scope.
25 < 1 
26 < 1 ## Steps
27 < 1 
28 < 1 1. **Branch.** From a clean `main`: `git switch -c chore/delete-comments-<YYYY-MM-DD>`.
29 < 1 2. **Inventory.** In the scratchpad, `python3 .claude/skills/delete-comment/scripts/inventory.py
30 < 1    <work> <shards> [path...]`. One shard per ~170 blocks, at most 12. It writes `blocks.json`
31 < 1    and `shards/shardNN.jsonl` (whole files per shard).
32 < 1 3. **Triage.** One `general-purpose` subagent per shard, all in one message, each told to read
33 < 1    and follow `.claude/skills/delete-comment/references/triage-brief.md` for its shard and to
34 < 1    write `<work>/out/shardNN.jsonl`. They never edit the repository. Check every id came back
35 < 1    once before going on.
36 < 1 4. **Spot-check.** Read 20 random deletions and every `keep`; overturn a verdict by editing
37 < 1    its line in `out/`.
38 < 1 5. **ADRs.** Group the `decision` verdicts by `adr_topic`, merging near-duplicate topics. Each
39 < 1    topic becomes or extends one `docs/adr/NNNN-<topic>.md` in the shape of
40 < 1    `docs/adr/README.md`; add it to the index there. Name symbols and files, never line numbers.
41 < 1 6. **Delete.** `python3 .claude/skills/delete-comment/scripts/apply.py <work>`. A `FAIL` line
42 < 1    is a comment it could not place; fix it by hand or mark it `keep`. Re-parse what changed:
43 < 1    `node --check` per `.mjs`/`.js`, `bun build --no-bundle` per `.ts`/`.tsx`.
44 < 1 7. **Issues.** Group the `excuse` verdicts by `issue_title`. Invoking this skill is the
45 < 1    operator's ask to file them: one `gh issue create --label comment-excuse` per title,
46 < 1    body = the drafted `issue_body` plus the file and symbol. Put the issue numbers in the PR.
47 < 1 8. **Ratchet.** `python3 lint/comments.py --update` (it refuses to raise a count), then the
48 < 1    gate: `python3 -m pytest`. A test that read a deleted comment's text is a `keep`: restore
49 < 1    that comment and re-run.
50 < 1 9. **PR.** One hand PR: categories with counts, ADRs added, issues filed, lines shed, and the
51 < 1    baseline total before and after. `gh pr merge --auto --squash`.
52 < 1 
53 < 1 ## Estimating
54 < 1 
55 < 1 `python3 lint/comments.py --json | python3 -c "import json,sys; print(sum(r['end']-r['start']+1
56 < 1 for r in map(json.loads, sys.stdin)))"` is the comment-line ceiling; trailing comments shed no
57 < 1 line, and each deleted block usually frees one blank line beside it.
58 < 1 